  "rules": [
    "Strong persistent underprediction in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show an upswing, add a positive level shift to the whole path (model is ~8–12 EUR too low on average in these examples).",
    "Trend/acceleration is under-modeled: true prices ramp faster than forecast. Apply an increasing uplift with horizon (small at day 1–3, larger by day 10–30).",
    "Forecasts show premature mean reversion/flattening: if history breaks upward (new local highs), suppress mean-reversion and keep an upward drift instead of reverting toward ~70.",
    "Lag error: the model follows the move but ~1–2 weeks late. In strong uptrends, shift the forecast trajectory earlier (or equivalently boost near-term more than the model does).",
    "Horizon-specific bias: near-term (days 1–5) underprediction is moderate, but medium/long horizon (days 10–30) underprediction is severe; use a piecewise correction with larger adjustments beyond ~day 7–10."
  ]
